592186049824 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049824 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428772 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186049824 #edb/ref 1031 "Logical Associative and Commutative Laws" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049824 #edb/ref 1033 2830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049824 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "16d9828c-8d8f-5f94-9530-7dc3e79040cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050128 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050128 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050128 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050128 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050128 #edb/ref 1031 "The Absorption Laws" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050128 #edb/ref 1033 2823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050128 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "2edfad38-c4ef-5df9-8b35-5ea30d354656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186157231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1031 "Logical Equivalence" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1033 2821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050777 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "65e4f73e-43a8-5089-914d-135e7396b995" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157078 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7079" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157078 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $X?$\n\n- $X \\land (Y \\lor X)$\n\n- $(X \\lor Y) \\land Y$\n\n- $(X \\lor Y) \\land X$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157078 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d91fdb8d-5a45-5ac2-a281-20dcbbd7d6ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157078 #edb/ref 1074 "The law that conjunction absorbs disjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nX \\land (X \\lor Y) \\equiv X.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $X.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X∧(Y∨X) & ≡X∧(X∨Y) \\\\  & ≡X.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $X.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(Y∨X)∧Y & ≡Y∧(Y∨X) \\\\  & ≡Y≢X.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is logically equivalent to $X.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(X∨Y)∧X & ≡X∧(X∨Y) \\\\  & ≡X.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157079 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7080" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157079 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are logically equivalent to $C?$\n\n- $(C \\land B) \\lor C$\n\n- $B \\lor (B \\land C)$\n\n- $C \\lor (C \\lor B)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "228d6823-70ab-5b04-807a-b87e5f98bccb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157079 #edb/ref 1074 "The law that disjunction absorbs conjunction is stated as\n\n$$\nC \\lor (C \\land B) \\equiv C.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is logically equivalent to $C.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(C∧B)∨C & ≡C∨(C∧B) \\\\  & ≡C.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is *not* logically equivalent to $C.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B∨(B∧C) & ≡B≢C.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is *not* logically equivalent to $C.$ This statement cannot be simplified using the absorption laws.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186157274 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218615